{# Which painter a plain canvas opens in, for the three dialogs that ask for
   one: the toolbar's (draw_dialog.jinja), a community's and a reply's. Neo
   Cucumber is the painter; Tegaki is kept for whoever wants it, behind a
   disclosure that starts closed. A closed <details> still submits what is in
   it, so the form says tool=neo unless Tegaki was picked.

   A two-tone community's dialogs do not include this: Tegaki knows nothing of
   the community's two colours. And Tegaki is offered to an account only: it
   uploads when it is done and keeps nothing on the device, so a guest's
   drawing would have nowhere to go. #}
{% if current_user %}
  <details class="community-draw-more">
    <summary>{{ ftl_get_message('community-drawing-other-painters') }}</summary>
    <label class="community-draw-choice">
      <input type="radio" name="tool" value="neo" checked /> Neo Cucumber
    </label>
    <label class="community-draw-choice">
      <input type="radio" name="tool" value="tegaki" /> Tegaki
    </label>
  </details>
{% else %}
  <input type="hidden" name="tool" value="neo" />
{% endif %}
